# Project Analysis

## Domain
LLM workflow orchestration engine — a Python CLI tool that manages multi-step, multi-coder delivery pipelines. It orchestrates AI coding agents (Claude, Codex, Qwen, DeepSeek) through structured workflows with review loops, automatic retries, and human-in-the-loop approval gates. The project is currently being enhanced with daemon mode and PostgreSQL-backed job management for asynchronous, long-running workflow execution.

## Tech Stack
- **Language:** Python 3.11+ with type hints and dataclasses
- **Package:** Setuptools-based, installable Python package (`agent-runner-v2`)
- **CLI:** Entry point `ukbe-run-agent` via `project.scripts`
- **Database:** PostgreSQL (for upcoming daemon mode — `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` job claiming)
- **LLM Integrations:** Claude Code CLI, OpenAI Codex CLI, Qwen Code CLI, DeepSeek API
- **Testing:** pytest, pytest-cov
- **External APIs:** OpenAI API, Anthropic API, DeepSeek API
- **Auth:** Environment-variable API keys (OPENAI_API_KEY, DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)

## Complexity
advanced

## Recommended Workflow Scope
- SOP (WORKFLOW_SOP_v1.md) — already exists, fully detailed for advanced complexity
- Status Rules (DELIVERY_STATUS_RULES_v1.md) — already exists, comprehensive lifecycle rules
- All 7 delivery templates (initiative, plan, task graph, task, implementation plan, review, memory) — already scaffolded
- Agent system (AGENTS.md + 6+ agent contracts) — recommended for full advanced coverage
- Template registry — already exists
- Full refine/replan loops for SOP, templates, and agents — recommended given existing delivery infrastructure

## Recommended Agent Roles
- Planner (delivery plan creation)
- Task Decomposer (dependency-aware task graph generation)
- Implementation Planner (scoped implementation plans)
- Executor (implementation within approved scope)
- Reviewer (independent review of plans, implementations)
- Validator (final validation of behavior and contract compliance)
- Memory Manager (durable context, snapshots, supersession links)
- Architect (workflow policy, scope, approval gates — project owner role)
- Runner (automated state enforcement, budget, routing, sidecar validation)

## Delivery Folder Structure
Standard `docs/delivery/` structure — already established and actively used. No customization needed. Current structure includes: 00_templates/, 01_initiatives/, 02_plans/, 03_tasks/, 04_implementation_plans/, 05_reviews/, 06_memory/, 08_agents/ (partially scaffolded). Note: 07_master_prompts/ is explicitly deprecated and should not be created.

## Project-Specific SOP Considerations
- **meta.json sidecar is the ONLY communication channel** — no stdout JSON parsing, no markdown write-backs, no pre-invocation sidecar writes
- **Agent master prompts are deprecated** — workflow step configurations in `template_groups.py` serve as agent invocation contracts; do not create 07_master_prompts/
- **Daemon mode enhancement in progress** — PostgreSQL-backed job management with submit/status/worker/approve/reject/retry/cancel CLI commands; conservative v1 resume strategy (no automatic crash recovery)
- **Cross-project scaffolding supported** — `--target-project-root` allows scaffolding into any repository
- **Strict authority precedence** — Runner logic > SOP + Status Rules > Artifact metadata > Artifact body content
- **No phase skipping, no overwriting approved artifacts, no scope drift** — enforced by runner state machine
- **Budget and timeout enforcement** — runner checks before every agent invocation
- **Existing delivery docs are partially scaffolded** — templates, SOP, status rules, registry, and one active initiative (daemon mode) with approved plan and task graph already exist; SOP generation should respect and update existing docs rather than regenerate from scratch
- **Backward compatibility required** — existing direct CLI execution path must be preserved alongside new daemon mode
- **Testing without LLM calls** — tests must use mocked providers or fixture-based workflows

